<title>SINGAPORE: OUB Bank 1996 net rises 19.7 pct.</title>
<headline>OUB Bank 1996 net rises 19.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			310.40   vs  259.33</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		  7.0    vs    7.0</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)	    45.65   vs   41.46</p>
<p>    Interest income (billions)    1.94   vs    1.53</p>
<p>    Group interest expense (blns)     1.26 vs    0.98</p>
<p>    Group net interest income	 678.15 vs  550.25</p>
<p>    Group fees and commissions	142.58 vs  128.51</p>
<p>    Group dividends			16.43 vs   13.95</p>
<p>    Group operating expenses	  432.71 vs  370.62</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax			 437.69 vs  370.40</p>
<p>    Group tax			     118.56 vs  105.03</p>
<p>    Group minorities			8.71 vs    6.05</p>
<p>    Bank net profit		     238.44 vs  193.75</p>
<p>    Bank net interest income	  502.19 vs  413.52</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: 30 May 1997</p>
<p>Last day register open: 19 May 1997</p>
<p>- Full name is Overseas Union Bank Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
